ptimize), and _PyImport_FrozenBootstrap, _PyImport_FrozenStdlib"] [94 1 "// and _PyImport_FrozenTest (Python/frozen.c's const struct _frozen *, each pointing to its table: name, code, size,"] [95 1 "// is_package, 24 bytes an entry, a zero entry last; the code is the frozen module's marshalled code object, its name"] [96 1 "// and code kept in the world). 0 for any other name, or when the data cannot be made."] [144 1 "// cbuf is a ctypes object's own memory: size bytes of the world's heap, zeroed, freed when the Go value it belongs to"] [145 1 "// is collected (the free queued on the library, run before its next call, as arbace/clib's Defer)."] [161 1 "// keepBytes is a copy of b in the world's memory with a terminating NUL (a bytes object passed as char *: CPython"] [162 1 "// hands C the object's own buffer; here its copy, kept alive by the ctypes object that holds it)."] [164 2 "// zeroed past the data for a wchar_t's width (queue 594: test_capi's PyUnicodeWriterTest.test_widechar reads b''"] [165 2 "// with a negative size, wcslen over it, as CPython's bytes' padding after ob_sval ends it)"] [173 1 "// keepWide is s as a NUL-terminated wchar_t string (UTF-32, ci's wchar_t) in the world's memory."] [184 1 "// The keep object a setter returns (the ctypes object's b_objects holds it): a buffer kept alive."] [191 1 "// The handles' reference counts (queue 262; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 262\"): a proxy's ob_refcnt counts"] [192 1 "// the references C holds, Python's own references being Go's. A proxy is made with count 0 (a borrowed reference: an"] [193 1 "// argument, a container's item); a new reference C receives raises it (newRef), Py_DecRef lowers it. A proxy whose"] [194 1 "// count is 0 is released when the outermost C entry ends (capiLeave: a ctypes foreign call, an extension module's"] [195 1 "// function, its PyInit), after the result was taken: its map entries dropped (the object is Go's again alone) and its"] [196 1 "// memory freed. A borrowed reference is so valid until the Python code that called C runs again, as CPython's while"] [197 1 "// its owner holds it. Types and the singletons are immortal (never released): their count is CPython's"] [198 1 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT, which Include/refcount.h's inline Py_INCREF leaves alone (>= it) and Py_DECREF too"] [199 1 "// (_Py_IsImmortal: >= _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT)."] [201 24 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT (64 bits)"] [202 24 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT"] [206 19 "// the proxies whose count was 0 at some point since the last release"] [207 19 "// the C entries in progress (capiEnter, capiLeave), every thread's"] [208 2 "// capiDepths are each Python thread's C entries in progress (py-regress-1127): its thread state's context is taken"] [209 2 "// back at its own outermost return"] [213 1 "// The C entries by thread (py-cthreads-1127): while another thread's C is suspended in Python code (the GIL handed"] [214 1 "// over inside a native's callback), cDepth stays above 0, so the proxies of count 0, the strings handed to C and the"] [215 1 "// C-born objects Go collected waited for every thread to be out of C at once (capiLeave at cDepth 0). Threads that each"] [216 1 "// spend their time in C (4 threads pickling with the C _pickle, its reducers sleeping) never are: the proxies grew"] [217 1 "// with all the work done, and refreshSizes after every native and the mirrors' synchronization at every entry with"] [218 1 "// them (thr.py, 4 threads: 349 s, 1 thread: 13 s). So each thread's outermost entry has a number (entryOf, from"] [219 1 "// entrySeq; the thread's next entry's when it is handed a handle before it enters, a native's arguments), every handle"] [220 1 "// given to C (handle) records the range of the entries it was given to (recv), and a thread's own outermost return"] [221 1 "// releases the proxies of count 0 no other live entry may hold borrowed (no live entry in its range) and the strings"] [222 1 "// its own entries were handed (keep); the C-born objects Go collected are deallocated at any thread's outermost entry."] [223 1 "// The release of every proxy of count 0 and the pending calls stay at cDepth 0, as before."] [225 32 "// the last entry's number"] [226 32 "// each thread's live (or next) outermost entry"] [227 32 "// the running thread's (entryOf's, 0: none yet; set at the GIL's hand-off, cThreadSwitch)"] [229 2 "// traversing is a tp_traverse's run (cTraverse): no reaping or releasing in it"] [233 1 "// openEntry is the running thread's entry: its live one, else a new number for its next; 0 (none: nothing recorded)"] [234 1 "// for a C thread's (PyThread_start_new_thread's, whose handles are released as before, at cDepth 0)."] [250 1 "// received records that the running thread's entry was given the handle a."] [270 1 "// heldElsewhere reports whether a live entry (the returning thread's taken out of entryOf) may hold the handle a:"] [271 1 "// one in the range of those it was given to."] [285 1 "// handle is o's PyObject *: its proxy's address (made on the first use: ob_refcnt 0, or immortal for a type; ob_type"] [286 1 "// its type's handle), recorded as given to the running thread's entry (received)."] [304 21 "// a C-born object (queue 268): its memory"] [307 27 "// a C type's instance over a built-in base (queue 269): its memory"] [310 2 "// the head of a PyVarObject (Include/object.h): ob_refcnt, ob_type and ob_size, which the limited API's inline"] [311 2 "// Py_SIZE reads (queue 262: PySlice_GetIndicesEx's macro over a list); since queue 269 a type's PyTypeObject and"] [312 2 "// a tuple's, list's, bytes' or float's mirror (capi_mirror.go)"] [319 33 "// a C metaclass's instance (queue 270b): its C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject"] [326 24 "// queue 521: PyModuleObject, md_state read in place"] [330 27 "// queue 568: PyCMethodObject, PyCFunction_GET_SELF and GET_FUNCTION read in place"] [334 13 "// PyStructObject: s_size, s_len, s_codes, s_format, weakreflist (queue 473: _testbuffer's get_nmemb)"] [360 29 "// a type, or a small int (CPython's are immortal: -5 to 256, queue 269)"] [365 35 "// ob_type: its type's handle"] [377 1 "// fromHandle is the object a PyObject * names (nil for NULL or an address that is no proxy)."] [385 23 "// queue 521: a static object of a C type (datetime's utc_timezone)"] [393 1 "// incRef and decRef are Py_IncRef and Py_DecRef on a handle (NULL and the immortal left alone)."] [419 1 "// steal takes C's reference to o's proxy for Python (a new reference C returned: Go holds the object from now on)."] [422 1 "// pin is a reference C's memory keeps for the process (a py_object stored into a ctypes object's memory, or returned"] [423 1 "// by a callback: CPython's object is kept by the ctypes object's _objects, which pyi's handles cannot follow)."] [430 1 "// unpinWith gives the pin of the handle h back once holder is collected (on the library's next call, as cbuf's free)."] [436 1 "// capiEnter and capiLeave bracket a C entry from Python: capiLeave of the outermost releases the proxies C no longer"] [437 1 "// holds and the strings PyArg_ParseTuple handed C. Usage: defer capiLeave(capiEnter())."] [447 3 "// the C-born objects Go collected: their tp_dealloc (queue 268), inside the entry (queue 473: a dealloc that"] [448 3 "// enters C again, ndarray_dealloc's PyBuffer_Release of a view, must not leave the outermost entry and release"] [449 3 "// the handles this entry's caller just made for it); at the thread's outermost entry (py-cthreads-1127: not only"] [450 3 "// the world's, which threads that are all in C never make)"] [456 1 "// reapAtCollect is py's ExtReap (a collection's rounds, finalize.go; py-breaker-1126): the C-born objects Go collected"] [457 1 "// deallocated now, in an entry of their own (capiEnter's reapDead, capiLeave releasing what they held), not at the world's"] [458 1 "// next entry; nothing inside a C entry (a collection C or its callback started: the outermost entry reaps)."] [461 12 "// inside this thread's C entry (py-cthreads-1127: another thread's suspended one reaps nothing away)"] [484 4 "// queue 594: tstate->context taken back when C returns (cleared by C: the thread's cleared); the thread's own"] [485 4 "// outermost return (py-regress-1127: another thread's C may still be suspended, cDepth above 0)"] [491 25 "// what no other live entry may hold (py-cthreads-1127)"] [498 2 "// a thread out of C that was given handles for its next entry (a call's arguments) keeps them"] [501 33 "// no entry lives: no handle is any entry's (a new map: clear's cost is its capacity's)"] [504 21 "// Py_AddPendingCall's, when C has returned to Python (py-capi-1122)"] [508 1 "// releaseUnowned releases every proxy of count 0 (outside any C entry); with partial (a thread's outermost return while"] [509 1 "// another thread's C entry lives, py-cthreads-1127) those no live entry may hold (heldElsewhere), and only the strings"] [510 1 "// of the entries that ended, the others kept in unowned."] [524 2 "// a free runs the library's deferred work first (unpinWith's), which may add to the list: taken before; a"] [525 2 "// mirror released gives its items back, which may release them too (queue 269): until none is left"] [548 14 "// a C-born object's memory is its own: freed by its tp_dealloc once Go collects it (queue 268)"] [551 5 "// so is a C type's instance over a built-in base (queue 269); its mirror leaves the map (py-regress2-1127),"] [552 5 "// kept by its born record for bornHandle to put back: the map's mirror held the instance (mr.o), so Go never"] [553 5 "// collected it and its tp_dealloc never ran (datetime's isocalendar() left an IsoCalendarDate and its three"] [554 5 "// ints mirrored a call, and syncAllToC and syncAllFromC walked them all at every entry: test_datetime's"] [555 5 "// ZoneInfoTest_Fast.test_gaps past its 300 s in the module's order, 11 s alone)"] [570 1 "// varProxies are the proxies of the mutable variable-size objects (dicts, 